I"¸<p>Spoken communication enables us to share thoughts, learn and create knowledge. Often we spend our day immersed in <em>listening to</em> or <em>speaking in</em> a conversation. Some conversations are quick and some <em>go on and on</em>, some start gradually and some end abruptly. Our goal is to explore spoken conversations by capturing and analyzing the speech, facial, breathing, heart and pupil signals of the participating individuals. This is a long-term effort involving building and testing several hypotheses, and gaining scientific insights into this amazing form of information transfer. Strength permitting, we will also analyze this aspect in bird (and animal) communication.</p>
